# Generated by `npm run db:types` from the local database, byte for byte as the Supabase
# CLI emits it. The CLI emits double quotes and no semicolons, against a config of
# singleQuote + semi — so without this entry the very next `npm run format` rewrites the
# file and tests/database-types.test.ts fails on the run after that, and keeps failing.
# That is the immediate cost; the standing one is that formatting would put a second
# definition of "correct" between the generator and the check, making the committed file
# a function of the Prettier version too, so a Prettier upgrade would read as a schema
# change. Still type-checked — tsconfig includes it, it is only the formatter and the
# linter that look away.
src/lib/database.types.ts
package-lock.json
LICENSE
NOTICE
src/assets/fonts/licenses/

